  "limitations": [
    "The retained pure checker and in-memory quantity authority are executable, including a deliberately full-resolution-only pending reservation slice and an ordered same-owner batch of at most 64 postings, but governed pack activation, partial pending resolution, automatic deadline enforcement, inventory capacity, account graphs, normalized tables, and a same-transaction CALA/general-action bridge are not production-bound.",
    "Lean and Kani currently prove independent reference functions, not production Rust correspondence; the quantity-unit/dimension lane also assumes ontology-artifact authenticity and SHA-256 collision resistance.",
    "The Quint lifecycle model omits storage, owner versions, idempotency maps, account floors, and partial-post policy; the separate authority model adds bounded owner/retry/record-count behavior but still abstracts storage as atomic assignments and treats authorization of the seal as a Boolean."
  ],
